<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Price decline prompts sales.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Price decline prompts sales.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rail soymeal sales increased slightly early Tuesday in reaction to lower CBOT soymeal futures, with most of the buying for immediate shipment, cash dealers said.</p>
<p>However, once CBOT soymeal futures turned higher later Tuesday morning, buyer interest waned.</p>
<p>Truck sales were slow as Midwest farmers concentrated on spring planting rather than buying livestock feed.</p>
<p>Crush margins remained poor and downtime for maintenance has been common. A southern Minnesota crusher will be down four to five days this week for maintenance, dealers said.  </p>
